-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",82,{
[2593]="7005479B\n1\tDefeat those shades who operate the Shrouded Forge\tBúrzangh, the Shrouded Forge, can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should defeat those who operate the Shrouded Forge.\n2\tDefeat the Spirit Forger\030Defeat the Forsaken Miner\030Defeat the Wayward Acolyte\tBúrzangh, the Shrouded Forge, can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should defeat those shades who operate the Shrouded Forge.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated those who operate the Shrouded Forge.\n",
[2594]="7005A954\n1\tDefeat bats and destroy their perches at Búshatap\tBúshatap can be found in Máttugard. You should defeat bats and destroy their perches at Búshatap.\n2\tDefeat bats at Búshatap (total: 10)\030Destroy bat perches at Búshatap (total: 10)\tBúshatap can be found in Máttugard. You should defeat bats and destroy their perches at Búshatap.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated bats and destroyed their perches at Búshatap.\n",
[2595]="70061388\n1\tClotild's bothersome neighbours can be found in various places throughout Gamwich. You should scold them for harassing her.\t\n2\tTalk to Clotild\tYou have properly scolded Clotild's neighbours. You should let her know.\n3\tTalk to Lassa in Tighfield\tClotild has asked you to let Lassa know she'll be arriving shortly. You should return to Tighfield to pass on the good news.\n",
[2596]="70022A72\n1\tExamine the rune\030Find the Rangers' rune hidden on an overlook above the curious ruins north-west of Lhanuch\tThe cache is somewhere a short distance north-west of Lhanuch where you can see a small set of curious ruins. You should be able to find the Rangers' rune on an overlook above them. Culang has sent you to find a cache of arrows, which can be found sixty paces south of a Rangers' rune.\n2\tDig here\030Search for the cache about sixty paces south of the Rangers' rune at the base of a small cliff.\tThe cache of arrows is buried about sixty paces directly south of the Rangers' rune, along the base of a small cliff there. Culang asked you to find a hidden cache of arrows.\n3\tTake the arrows to Culang in Nan Laeglin\tCulang is at his camp in Nan Laeglin, south-east of the cache. You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the arrows hidden there. Now you should return with them to Culang.\n",
[2597]="70022A74\n1\tExamine the rune\030Find the Rangers' rune hidden on a solitary tree east of Lhanuch\tThe cache of bandages he says is hidden east of Lhanuch. The rune-marker should be carved on a solitary tree somewhere directly east of the Lhanuch. Culang has sent you to retrieve a hidden cache of bandages.\n2\tDig here\030The cache should be buried in a small copse of trees north-east of the Rangers' rune\tThe cache of bandages is buried in a small copse of trees directly north-east of the rune. Culang asked you to retrieve a hidden cache of bandages.\n3\tBring the bandages to Culang\tCulang is at his camp in Nan Laeglin, to the south of the cache. You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the bandages hidden there. Now you should return with them to Culang.\n",
[2598]="70022A73\n1\tExamine the rune\030Find the rune atop a green hill with several trees upon it\tThe cache of healing draughts is hidden well to the south of Lhanuch, on the border of the Lich Bluffs. The Rangers' rune may be found atop a green hill with many trees upon it. Culang has sent you to retrieve a hidden cache of healing draughts.\n2\tDig here\030Find the Rangers' cache forty paces west of the rune, buried around a boulder among a stand of evergreens\tThe cache of potions would be buried around the base of a boulder some forty paces west into a stand of evergreens. Culang asked you to retrieve a hidden cache of healing draughts.\n3\tBring the healing draughts to Culang\tCulang is at his camp in Nan Laeglin, north-east of the cache. You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the healing draughts hidden there. Now you should return with them to Culang.\n",
[2599]="70022733\n1\tExamine the rune\030Find the hidden rune\tBraigiar has pointed you to a cache of foodstuffs he says is hidden in the north-western area of Fordirith. He believes it should be buried about twenty paces west from a tree marked with the Ranger's rune.\n2\tDig here\030Find the Rangers' cache of foodstuffs\tBraigiar said the cache of foodstuffs would be buried about twenty paces west of the rune-marked tree.\n3\tTake the food to Braigiar\tBraigiar is at Echad Dagoras in Fordirith. You discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the foodstuffs hidden there. Now you should return with them to Braigiar.\n",
[2600]="70022747\n1\tExamine the rune\030Find the hidden rune\tAmarion has pointed you to a cache of weapon-lore scrolls he says is hidden within the Black Dens, south-east of Echad Dagoras. He believes it should be buried about fifty paces west of the cavern floor marked with the Rangers' rune.\n2\tDig here\030Find the Rangers' cache of scrolls\tAmarion said the cache of weapon-lore scrolls would be buried about fifty paces west of the rune-marked cavern.\n3\tTake the scrolls to Amarion\tAmarion is at Echad Dagoras, north-west of the Black Dens. You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the scrolls of lore hidden there. Now you should return with them to Amarion.\n",
[2601]="70022732\n1\tExamine the rune\030Find the hidden rune\tBraigiar has pointed you to a cache of herbs and poultices he says is hidden in the north-eastern area of Fordirith. He believes it should be buried among a stand of pine trees eighty paces north of a boulder marked with the Rangers' rune.\n2\tDig here\030Find the Rangers' medicine cache\tBraigiar said the cache of medicines would be buried among a grove of pine trees roughly eighty paces north of a large rune-marked boulder.\n3\tTake the medicines to Braigiar\tBraigiar is at Echad Dagoras, south-west of the medicine-cache. You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the medicines hidden there. Now you should return with them to Braigiar.\n",
[2602]="7002270F\n1\tExamine the rune\030Find the hidden rune\tBraigiar has pointed you to a cache he believes is hidden in the Southern area of Fordirith. First, you should find a marker rune atop a small rounded hill with several trees upon it.\n2\tDig here\030Find the Rangers' weapons-cache\tBraigiar said the cache of weapons would be buried about sixty paces east of the rune marker, amid a jumble of large boulders.\n3\tTake the weapons to Braigiar\tBraigiar is at Echad Dagoras, north of the weapon-cache. You have discovered the Rangers' cache and dug up the weapons hidden there. You should return with them to Braigiar.\n",
[2603]="70046C2A\n1\tUncover buried caches in North Ithilien (total: 8)\tBuried caches can be found to the north of Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien. Tordoron has asked you to search the lands to the north of Henneth Annûn for buried caches.\n2\tDeliver the caches to Tordoron\tTordoron can be found in the northern wilds of North Ithilien. You have recovered several caches from the north lands of Ithilien and should now deliver them to Tordoron.\n",
[2604]="7005B4BD\n1\tDestroy crystal caches (total: 10)\tCaches of corrupted crystals can be found in central Clovengap. You should destroy any caches of sarrowstone crystals you come across.\n2\tReturn to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is in Bazanmanar in north-eastern Clovengap. You should let Mother Amma know you have taken care of the crystals.\n",
[2605]="70054683\n1\tBlock small passages (total: 8)\tMany small passages exist within Torech Ungol, allowing the spiders and gredbyg to come and go. You should block these small passages to trap Shelob's brood.\n",
[2606]="70046BE3\n1\tFind Molvagúr\tMolvagúr, captain of the Enemy forces at Cair Andros, is somewhere on the island. You should find Molvagúr.\n2\tDefeat Molvagúr\tMolvagúr, is on Cair Andros. You should defeat Molvagúr.\n3\tTalk to Duinhir near Cair Andros\tDuinhir can be found near Cair Andros. You should speak to Duinhir.\n",
[2607]="70046BE0\n1\tDefeat Maushlak\tMaushlak, an Uruk cook, is holding captives to vie for power at Cair Andros. You should defeat Maushlak.\n2\tCaptives are being held at Cair Andros. You should rescue the captives.\t\n3\tTalk to Duinhir near Cair Andros\tDuinhir can be found near Cair Andros. You should speak to Duinhir.\n",
[2608]="70046BDF\n1\tDefeat Orc scouts (total: 8)\tDefeat Orc scouts on the fortress walls around Cair Andros.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated Orc scouts.\n",
[2609]="70046BDE\n1\tDestroy weapon-racks (total: 10)\tWeapon-racks can be found around Cair Andros. You should destroy weapon-racks.\n2\tCompleted\tDestroy weapon-racks.\n",
[2610]="700032A5\n1\tTalk to Calengil\tCalengil can be found in the Elf-refuge of Duillond to the north. Thinglaer has asked you to seek out his brother Calengil and lend him what aid you may.\n",
[2611]="70009791\n1\tBring Aragorn's letter to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at Tinnudir, an island on the eastern shore of Lake Nenuial, in Evendim, far to the west of the Trollshaws. Aragorn has given you a letter to present to Calenglad and advice concerning the nature of respect: that it cannot be bought, but must be earned. With the aid of Calenglad, Aragorn hopes that you can recover the Silithar needed to reforge Narsil.\n",
[2612]="7002BF97\n1\tTalk to the captain of the shades at Atburg in the Rushgore\tThe captain of the shades is somewhere at Atburg, south-east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore. Wynstan has asked you to convince the captain of the shades to rejoin the fight against the Enemy and fulfill his oath.\n2\tComplete Stolen Pride and obtain the good will of the shades\tRelics can be found at Atburg and upon the brigands therein. Brúngwath has asked you to complete Aculf's request and collect the stolen relics to show your honour.\n3\tTalk to Eowils outside Atburg in the Rushgore\tEowils is outside Atburg in the Rushgore, south-east of Aculf's camp. Wynstan told you to report your successes to the scout Eowils.\n",
[2613]="7003A667\n1\tGo up into the tower and witness the view at the Halifirien\tThe tower high atop Beaconwatch is where Lady Answith is awed by the view of the Halifirien. Lady Answith recommended that you view the Halifirien and thus perhaps learn to understand her husband's devotion.\n2\tTalk to Lady Answith\tLady Answith is on a porch above the vendor's area north of the Mead Hall in Beaconwatch. After witnessing the breathtaking view of the Halifirien, you have an idea of the sense of duty that Cútha has for keeping watch. You should return to Lady Answith and tell her that you have gazed upon the Halifirien from high atop Beaconwatch.\n",
[2614]="70057181\n1\tTalk to Grimbeorn at the Beorninghús\tGrimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús in the Vales of Anduin. You should talk to Grimbeorn.\n",
[2615]="7000B3DF\n1\tPlace the thistledown haunches on the flat stone in the Isendeep\030Collect thistledown haunches (total: 5)\tSearch the areas south of Tol Ascarnen or west along the plains south and west of Dâr-gazag for the thistledown grazers. Collect some of their haunches and bring them to the slab within the depths of the Isendeep. Soldier Golb directed you to turn the force of drakes often found stalking the Isendeep Mines against the Free People. He wants you to draw the drakes in with the promise of aurochs meat.\n",
[2616]="70040CF2\n1\tTalk to Malthellam in Morlad\tMalthellam can be found outside his home in Morlad. Gúrion asks that you return to Malthellam in Morlad to warn him of the impending union between the Dead and the invader from Tarlang's Crown.\n2\tArchers can be found along the borders of Morlad in Blackroot Vale. Malthellam has asked you to send an archer to each of the villages in Blackroot Vale to aid in their defence.\t\n3\tTalk to Malthellam\tMalthellam can be found outside his home in Morlad. You have rallied an archer to the defence of each of Blackroot Vale's villages and should now report back to Malthellam.\n",
[2617]="70058BC6\n1\tTalk to Náin the Slakeless at Drenghól\tNáin the Slakeless can be found at the hidden refuge of Drenghól in the northern reaches of Elderslade during the War of Three Peaks. Náin the Slakeless has led a company north toward Bagûd-mekhem in attempt to secure a forward encampment outside Mount Gundabad. You should muster at Drenghól and report to Náin the Slakeless.\n",
[2618]="7006C532\n1\tAssist Andur in seeing his bloodline survives beyond him\030Assist Meliri in putting her husband's spirit to rest\030Help Zidek achieve vengeance for all he lost\tZidemel asked you to assist three adherents to appease the spirit of the desert, Ishími. Assist Meliri, Zidek, and Andur. They are all in attendance Zidemel preaches.\n2\tReturn to Zidemel to tell him you aided his flock\tYou aided Zidemel's followers to complete the appeasement of the spirits. You should return to Zidemel in Jirush, located in central Khûd Zagin, to tell him that have aided his adherents.\n",
[2619]="70000D9B\n1\tTalk to Hart Holeman\tHart Holeman is at his home in the centre of Overhill. Hyacinth Took appreciated the saltpetre you brought back with you, though she chided you for letting Cam Puddifoot talk you into hunting wolves for him. Now she has asked you to speak with Hart Holeman about the charcoal she needs.\n",
[2620]="70027203\n1\tTalk to Gwilum in Barnavon\tGwilum is at Barnavon-town, far to the west of the Barnavon Mine. Melvun asked you to go to Gwilum and ask for replacement workers.\n",
[2621]="7006BF6B\n1\tFind and call Ninda home for supper\030Find and call Shûbar home for supper\030Find and call Zâli home for supper\030Find and call Ladûl home for supper\tCall the children Ninda, Shûbar, Zâli, and Ladûl home to Entârshul in Urmâkh for supper. Entârshul suggests telling them Shangarûd will find them if they are reticent to come home. They can be found inside and just outside the gates of Urmâkh.\n2\tSpeak with Entârshul in Urmâkh\tSpeak with Entârshul in Urmâkh.\n",
[2622]="700007B5\n1\tDefeat wights in the northern Barrow-downs (total: 12)\tWights can be found throughout the Barrow-downs, east and north of the guides' camp. Through their own folly, the guides have become trapped. While here they wish to assist the Watchers of Bree by reducing the threat found in the Barrow-downs.\n2\tTalk to Reginald Sickleweed in the Barrow-downs\tYou will find Reginald Sickleweed at the makeshift camp between the Old Forest and the northern Barrow-downs. You should now return to Reginald Sickleweed and tell him that you have begun to purge the wights from the Barrow-downs.\n",
[2623]="700330CB\n1\tDefeat Orcs at the Crack's Edge (total: 8)\tOrcs can be found at the Crack's Edge along the great rift in the centre of Nud-melek. You should defeat Orcs at the Crack's Edge outpost.\n2\tReturn to Svanr\tSvanr is at the west side of the chasm upon the Bridge of Khazad-dûm in Nud-melek. You should tell Svanr that have defeated a number of Orcs at the Crack's Edge.\n",
[2624]="70047AE6\n1\tEnter the Towers of the Teeth\tThe Towers of the Teeth are located in the Slag-hills. You should destroy camp-tents in the Towers of the Teeth.\n2\tDestroy tents within the Towers of the Teeth (total: 12)\tThe Towers of the Teeth are located in the Slag-hills. You should destroy camp-tents in the Towers of the Teeth.\n3\tCompleted\tDestroyed many tents in the Towers of the Teeth.\n",
})
